00:02:59,953 --> 00:03:04,813
Mark 33! Do not let him pass! We can't let that fullback have free reign!

72
00:03:06,293 --> 00:03:08,473
Why are we marking a wimp like Aoi?

73
00:03:11,753 --> 00:03:14,913
Come on, Kurada! Just give me the frickin' ball this time!

74
00:03:15,913 --> 00:03:19,053
Why when you're being marked? Do you have something in mind?

75
00:03:25,093 --> 00:03:27,753
What the heck? He hit it right back to me?

76
00:03:29,393 --> 00:03:33,353
There's not any spin on it, so it's easy to keep it at my feet.

77
00:03:34,433 --> 00:03:36,613
Is he wanting me to just hold it here?

78
00:03:38,253 --> 00:03:43,693
Think, Kurada, think! Since the ball is at your feet, you're free to check out where all the spaces are!

79
00:03:45,253 --> 00:03:49,093
You got this! You can set up a move wherever you send the ball!

80
00:03:53,593 --> 00:03:57,713
Oh, I get it now! Back during the Inner Squad match in April.

81
00:03:57,713 --> 00:04:00,013
The type of pass should have clued you in right away.

82
00:04:00,013 --> 00:04:04,873
I wondered what the heck he was talking about. Makes sense now.

83
00:04:04,873 --> 00:04:12,333
On top of making eye contact and barking instructions, I can also send different messages with the types of passes I make.

84
00:04:12,933 --> 00:04:18,293
I thought I knew everything. Then something clicked. There's so much more to soccer than I realized.

85
00:04:19,513 --> 00:04:24,293
What the... He's pushed all the way up here? Does he not know he's a fullback?

86
00:04:24,293 --> 00:04:27,893
No. No. No. He's been very useful today.

87
00:04:28,513 --> 00:04:31,013
His positioning may be bizarre, but I can tell he's got a plan.

88
00:04:33,213 --> 00:04:34,673
Sugawara! Coming back to you!

89
00:04:34,673 --> 00:04:37,653
Just keep it there!

90
00:04:41,233 --> 00:04:46,533
I'm moving them. It's all rearranged. Because of me, everything changed.

91
00:04:47,633 --> 00:04:48,193
Awesome.

92
00:04:49,573 --> 00:04:53,713
There's a perfect way to score. And you're the only one capable of it.

93
00:04:56,513 --> 00:04:57,073
Owie!

94
00:04:57,073 --> 00:05:04,353
Point the toes of my planted foot where I want it to go.

95
00:05:04,933 --> 00:05:07,493
Then hit the middle of the ball with the top of my foot.

96
00:05:08,873 --> 00:05:10,153
They switched to play?

97
00:05:12,153 --> 00:05:14,073
It's like the field...

98
00:05:14,073 --> 00:05:15,853
just became part of me!

99
00:05:21,933 --> 00:05:23,913
What? Another diagonal?

100
00:05:23,913 --> 00:05:29,033
That's the second time. An unplanned diagonal run by a fullback.

101
00:05:29,653 --> 00:05:32,613
That tricky goal they conceded is still fresh in their minds.

102
00:05:33,233 --> 00:05:34,793
No way they come out strong.

103
00:05:35,673 --> 00:05:37,413
Why is no one putting pressure on him?

104
00:05:37,933 --> 00:05:39,273
Yeah! I've got him!

105
00:05:40,033 --> 00:05:40,553
Here!

106
00:05:42,753 --> 00:05:43,613
I hear you!

107
00:05:44,273 --> 00:05:46,813
I'm more of a cautious, sensible type of player.

108
00:05:47,133 --> 00:05:49,273
So high-risk diagonal runs aren't really my thing.

109
00:05:49,713 --> 00:05:50,713
I never do them.

110
00:05:50,713 --> 00:05:55,333
But when you switched the play earlier, the moment you kicked the ball,

111
00:05:55,673 --> 00:05:57,393
you looked right at me and I knew.

112
00:05:57,773 --> 00:05:59,373
That smile just screamed,

113
00:05:59,673 --> 00:06:01,213
let's go kick their asses!

114
00:06:01,473 --> 00:06:01,773
Right?

115
00:06:02,333 --> 00:06:04,013
Huh? Another diagonal run?

116
00:06:07,513 --> 00:06:09,093
Whoa! That was sweet, Ajito!

117
00:06:09,353 --> 00:06:10,113
Now we're open!

118
00:06:12,913 --> 00:06:14,493
Even when he's at that range,

119
00:06:14,913 --> 00:06:16,773
Owie would normally try to force a shot.

120
00:06:16,773 --> 00:06:19,313
He's almost to the vine line!

121
00:06:19,913 --> 00:06:20,693
What was it?

122
00:06:22,313 --> 00:06:24,233
You called it a diagonal run?

123
00:06:24,593 --> 00:06:25,933
I think... maybe?

124
00:06:27,473 --> 00:06:28,213
That right?

125
00:06:28,973 --> 00:06:30,573
Running from the middle to right there?

126
00:06:34,153 --> 00:06:35,813
Watch the flank! Look out!

127
00:06:35,813 --> 00:06:41,933
Confusion.

128
00:06:42,453 --> 00:06:43,673
The secret sauce.

129
00:06:44,253 --> 00:06:46,613
If I can confuse the crap out of him like this,

130
00:06:47,073 --> 00:06:48,873
it doesn't matter who finishes it.

131
00:06:51,373 --> 00:06:53,053
And since it doesn't,

132
00:06:53,573 --> 00:06:54,593
it could be me.

133
00:06:54,593 --> 00:07:24,573
I actually scored.

134
00:07:24,573 --> 00:07:25,413
My boy, Ajito!

135
00:07:25,413 --> 00:07:26,313
It's been a while.

136
00:07:27,753 --> 00:07:29,033
That felt amazing!

137
00:07:30,413 --> 00:07:31,573
Give him one more hit!

138
00:07:31,653 --> 00:07:33,573
What kind of monster is he?

139
00:07:34,273 --> 00:07:36,293
He orchestrated all of that on his own.

140
00:07:36,873 --> 00:07:38,493
And he's still only a first year?

141
00:07:41,133 --> 00:07:43,053
The momentum's with us now.

142
00:07:46,573 --> 00:07:47,393
One goal!

143
00:07:47,853 --> 00:07:49,073
Just one goal behind!

144
00:07:49,073 --> 00:07:50,373
We've got this!

145
00:07:50,913 --> 00:07:52,373
Don't know about that.

146
00:07:53,233 --> 00:07:55,233
If you're trying to mark me out of the game,

147
00:07:55,313 --> 00:07:56,753
it's probably not gonna work.

148
00:07:58,493 --> 00:07:58,973
